      "message": "Cherry pick is not clean. Checked against UPSTREAM.\nUPSTREAM commit: [googlesource](https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/common/+/4efaa5acf0a1d2b5947f98abb3acf8bfd966422b) [kernel.org](https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id\u003d4efaa5acf0a1d2b5947f98abb3acf8bfd966422b).\n\n```\n      ## fs/eventpoll.c ##\n     @@ fs/eventpoll.c: static __poll_t __ep_eventpoll_poll(struct file *file, poll_table *wait, int dep\n      \treturn res;\n      }\n      \n    ++\n     +/*\n     + * The ffd.file pointer may be in the process of being torn down due to\n     + * being closed, but we may not have finished eventpoll_release() yet.\n    @@ fs/eventpoll.c: static __poll_t __ep_eventpoll_poll(struct file *file, poll_tabl\n      /*\n       * Differs from ep_eventpoll_poll() in that internal callers already have\n       * the ep-\u003emtx so we need to start from depth\u003d1, such that mutex_lock_nested()\n    -@@ fs/eventpoll.c: static __poll_t __ep_eventpoll_poll(struct file *file, poll_table *wait, int dep\n    - static __poll_t ep_item_poll(const struct epitem *epi, poll_table *pt,\n    +@@ fs/eventpoll.c: static __poll_t ep_item_poll(const struct epitem *epi, poll_table *pt,\n      \t\t\t\t int depth)\n      {\n    --\tstruct file *file \u003d epi-\u003effd.file;\n    + \tstruct file *file \u003d epi-\u003effd.file;\n     +\tstruct file *file \u003d epi_fget(epi);\n      \t__poll_t res;\n      \n```\n\n\nPlease refer to the contribution guidelines for details:\nhttps://android.googlesource.com/kernel/common/+/refs/heads/android-mainline/README.md",
